peana.eu/item/9200211/en_list_one_csg_1869"/><edm:dataProvider rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/organization/1482250000004502183"></edm:dataProvider><edm:isShownAt rdf:resource="http://www.e-codices.unifr.ch/en/list/one/csg/1869"/><edm:isShownBy rdf:resource="http://www.e-codices.unifr.ch/loris/csg/csg-1869/csg-1869_001.jp2/full/full/0/default.jpg"/><edm:object rdf:resource="http://www.e-codices.unifr.ch/loris/csg/csg-1869/csg-1869_001.jp2/full/full/0/default.jpg"/><edm:provider rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/organization/1482250000004671163"></edm:provider><edm:rights rdf:resource="http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/3.0/"/></ore:Aggregation><ore:Proxy rdf:about="http://data.europeana.eu/proxy/provider/9200211/en_list_one_csg_1869"><dc:coverage>Dominican cloister St. Gall (Angela Varnbühler)</dc:coverage><dc:creator>Anselm von Canterbury</dc:creator><dc:date>around 1487</dc:date><dc:description>Composite manuscript with sermons and spiritual instructions, written around 1487 in the Dominican cloister St. Katharinen in St. Gall by the prioress Angela Varnbüeler. Among others, the volume contains a detailed sermon about Saint Clare of Assisi, into which is incorporated her vita; an open letter from a father to his spiritual children, attributed to a Franciscan monk; a sermon about suffering, death and the sacraments (an interpretation of John 16,21); and a meditation Von der Maß des gaistlichen Crutz, falsely attributed to Anselm of Canterbury.</dc:description><dc:format>532 pp., 15 x 10.5 cm</dc:format><dc:identifier>doi:10.5076/e-codices-csg-1869</dc:identifier><dc:identifier>http://www.e-codices.unifr.ch/en/list/one/csg/1869</dc:identifier><dc:identifier>St. Gallen, Stiftsbibliothek, Cod. Sang. 1869</dc:identifier><dc:publisher>e-codices - Virtual Manuscript Library of Switzerland</dc:publisher><dc:language>German</dc:language><dc:relation>Scarpatetti Beat Matthias von, Die Handschriften der Stiftsbibliothek St. Gallen, Codices 1726-1984 (14.-1